WEBVTT

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.860
MOBILE SUIT
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY</b>

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.060
Üso, behind you!

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:37.100
The death of Üso's mother was cruel.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:42.600
But with it came news that the war was over.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:49.530
Days without fighting would be kinder for people, but...

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:51.900
TWINRAD COUNTERATTACK

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:55.430
"Twinrad Counterattack".

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:17.830
An agricultural goods warehouse.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.230
It's big enough to hide a mobile suit.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:35.000
They say there's a ceasefire in effect,

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:38.230
but BESPA mobile suits are still on the move.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:39.730
What's going on?

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:41.900
Miss Marbet!

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:45.400
The Motorad Fleet's main force has returned to space.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:47.300
Even if we spot enemy movements,

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:49.530
we can't take any action first.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:51.160
I know.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:54.530
But I won't forgive the Motorad Fleet that killed my mother!

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.530
I understand how you feel,

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:59.100
but if you try fighting a personal vendetta,

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:01.130
then you can't pilot Victory!

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:04.700
A vendetta? That's not what I had in mind.

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:08.260
If the enemy's still on the move around here, the fighting will continue.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.330
Üso, you hear me? Üso!

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:12.200
We've got big news!

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:13.230
Can you hear me?

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:14.660
Okay, listen up!

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:17.230
They gave us leave! We can go home!

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:18.300
Give that back!

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:22.600
Üso, we're going back to Kasarelia!

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:23.630
Kasarelia?

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:26.800
Captain Gomez has authorized leave, huh?

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.100
It's proof they're abiding by the ceasefire.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:33.760
Now you can bury your mother in your homeland.

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:35.960
Yeah. It's really okay?

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:39.330
I'll ask Captain Gomez to let me come, too.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:53.360
You're headed for the Pacific, white mobile suits?

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:16.530
Okay, move it!

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:18.730
Left more! Left!

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:19.830
Stop!

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.100
Use the mobile suit's hand to...

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:23.200
Chief Cicely!

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:24.060
Sir!

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:27.530
Even taking that you're working in gravity into account, you're too slow!

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:28.860
It'll be done by the time we leave port.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:30.260
Get used to being on Earth.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:30.960
Sir!

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.530
Second Lieutenant Paloma has returned.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:33.430
Good!

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:40.930
Second Lieutenant Paloma has landed.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.460
Prepare to launch!

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:43.860
All hands, confirm position.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:48.900
What about the checks over here?

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:51.130
Cicely, you're still at it?

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:52.900
Yes. I'm sorry.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:57.330
Those white mobile suits are an enemy we have to destroy.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:58.760
Of course.

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:02.760
The homeland may have signed the ceasefire because they wanted time,

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:05.660
but as an engineer, it's a source of constant shame.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:09.900
The Motorad Fleet's original objective was Operation Earth Clean.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:13.800
Lieutenant Commander Iq doesn't do things by half measures,

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:15.960
hence this rematch we're planning.

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:17.100
Hurry the work!

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:17.930
Yes, ma'am!

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:35.860
Yahoo!

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.230
Fishing! Fishing!

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:39.400
I can't wait to see if I catch anything!

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:41.560
What's so fun about that?

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:43.360
Martina, you're getting distracted.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:44.600
Yeah, Martina.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:47.800
We'd be just as excited if we were headed home, right?

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:49.130
Can you do these, too?

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:50.730
Huh? All those?

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:54.500
You know, working in gravity tires us out.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:57.630
We can put up a grave stone. That'll be nice, right?

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:58.730
I know.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:01.530
Üso, can you take out the Gundam?

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:02.700
The Gundam?

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:05.960
Probably to help them fish. Do it.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.160
To fish?

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:11.230
It may take longer, but we shouldn't fly too high.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:14.900
Why not just head into the Mediterranean and turn north?

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:18.160
I don't want to cause any trouble with Arti Gibraltar...

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:20.960
...or remind those kids of what happened there.

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:26.860
Like this?

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:28.330
Great! Great!

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:30.630
What are you fishing for?

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.330
Something this big!

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:38.230
It doesn't matter, as long as it cheers Üso up.

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:40.260
You're right, Warren.

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:48.430
Okay, let's see if I can land some big game, too!

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:50.730
Hey! Miss Martina! Elisha! Come join us!

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:54.460
I don't like it out there. It smells like salt and it's sticky.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:57.230
I far prefer the smell of machine oil.

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:00.160
She doesn't like the smell of salt?

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:01.530
Really?

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:03.460
It doesn't make me sick.

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.800
Maybe it's the smell of living things rotting.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:08.630
It smells awful!

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:11.830
Sorry. Guess they're not used to Earth.

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:15.530
Does everyone who grows up in space feel that way?

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:17.130
I can't marry her!

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.530
It doesn't mean that!

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:21.430
It does if she can never get used to living on Earth!

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:23.360
You've thought it that far through?

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:26.530
But, I want to live on Earth!

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:30.730
Relax. It's not like you and Martina are even a couple.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:34.330
You don't have to be so mean about it!

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:36.030
Don't you think it'd be sad...

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:40.030
...if something like this tore two lovers apart?!

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:44.960
People born and raised in space don't like the smell of the sea.

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:48.400
The Zanscare probably feel the same.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:52.660
So, why'd they even come to Earth and kill my mom?

00:08:11.230 --> 00:08:11.900
What?

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:12.660
Huh?

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:13.830
That one really jumped high.

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.460
Missiles! Missiles!

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.030
Taking us up!

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:20.330
All hands, battle stations!

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:21.630
Where are they coming from?!

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:24.330
The enemy?!

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:26.030
Üso, where are they?!

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:33.160
Open a channel to the Reineforce Junior!

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:36.230
Üso! Odelo! Tomáš! Use your mobile suits to shoot down the missiles!

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:38.800
If the enemy's attacking, we'll just have to fight!

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:46.760
Understand? Don't leave the White Ark!

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:48.760
Gotcha. Incoming!

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:54.560
They're violating the agreement!

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:57.600
The Reineforce Junior is half a day away from you!

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:00.860
You can request support from Londonderry unit!

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:02.100
Right! Roger!

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:03.730
Hang on!

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:06.100
Something's surfacing behind us!

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:07.300
A Motorad vessel?

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:10.260
Looks like it. It looks like a Lysithea-class.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:13.330
The ship's appeared!

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:21.260
I can handle one ship!

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:22.130
What?!

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:26.660
They can operate on water, too?!

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:31.330
They're fast!

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:36.300
Don't waste ammo!

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:37.830
But, it's the white one!

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:39.760
We take out the carrier, first!

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:44.100
A mobile suit that's lost its home is no match for us!

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:49.560
They're going after the White Ark?!

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:55.860
It gets your biker blood pumping, right Renda? Cicely?

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:58.730
Yes, sir! Running like this is amazing!

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:02.800
I'm honored to pilot a unit I serviced myself!

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:04.660
The enemy ship's attacking!

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:12.360
They're moving too fast!

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:14.800
At this rate, we'll be a nice, fat target for them!

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:19.030
Odelo, Tomáš, protect the White Ark!

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:22.200
If worse comes to worst, you can be the White Ark's engines!

00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:23.960
Because we're in the atmosphere!

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:28.500
The shield!

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:31.030
Die!

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:34.560
Not bad!

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:40.560
Hit them! Hit them, please!

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:43.760
Just die!

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:48.430
The engine room!

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:51.600
Light damage. All hands, assume fire fighting operations!

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:52.860
Elisha! Martina!

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.160
We're putting them out!

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:56.030
We can still fire the mega particle cannon!

00:10:56.060 --> 00:10:57.100
Y-Yes, sir!

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:06.660
Just one direct hit, and their ship is done for! Damn their persistence!

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:11.730
The White Ark retreated?!

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:12.930
It's all right.

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:16.330
It won't sink. I think it's heading for that island.

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:22.730
Don't let it explode!

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:24.300
Get more foam at the base of the fire!

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:25.260
Like this?

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:26.460
That looks okay.

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:27.500
Thank goodness!

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:35.700
Shahkti!

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:38.100
I... I'm okay!

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:55.160
Thanks, Martina.

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:56.600
I'm glad you're okay.

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:58.700
Thanks, Flanders. You can let go, now.

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:01.260
Shahkti, you're bleeding!

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:03.230
It's just a scratch.

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:05.300
An island! We're coming to an island!

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:12.130
We've reached the coast?

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:14.260
Use the White Ark as a turret!

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:15.830
There are no rocks to use as a shield!

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:17.660
Tomáš, we're landing!

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:20.800
Tomáš! Once we land, we'll head out to fight, too!

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:21.900
R-Roger!

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:31.060
Should we really land in a place like this?

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:32.200
It stinks!

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:34.500
Sis, what are those white things?!

00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:36.530
They look like whale bones.

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:39.800
This rotting meat smell is horrible!

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:41.960
Shahkti, I feel sick.

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:42.960
Y-Yeah.

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:46.860
Do all these bleached bones that are washed up here...

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:49.460
...show how badly this ocean is polluted?

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:53.900
No! No! I don't want to stay here!

00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:57.560
I can't believe horrible places like this exist!

00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:00.130
Are they upset about how much the sea is polluted?

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:03.600
Afraid of how corpses rot and leave bones behind?

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:04.960
Which is it?

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:08.500
The White Ark's going to act as a gun turret!

00:13:12.030 --> 00:13:14.630
A mountain of bones gathered by the ocean currents?

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:17.730
I won't let you pollute the Earth anymore!

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:19.760
Odelo, don't do anything...

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:22.600
...that'll reveal the White Ark's position to the enemy.

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:23.800
Understood!

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:26.100
Maybe get Miss Elisha and the others off the ship!

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:27.930
What do we do, Dad?

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:30.730
Do it! Londonderry are on their way!

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:33.500
Warren, use this chance to reload our missiles!

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:35.560
I'm doing that right now!

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:43.200
If we die here, we'll rot like the fish and whales on this coast, leaving only our bones...

00:13:43.230 --> 00:13:45.160
...and the stench of death!

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:48.900
It's a horrible way to die!

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:51.960
Even I've never seen anything like this!

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:00.360
Unit 3, pick up the pace!

00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:01.800
The white one!

00:14:01.830 --> 00:14:03.560
Why do you have to chase us?!

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.060
Üso broke up their team play!

00:14:12.730 --> 00:14:15.360
We may get a huge wave hitting us in second!

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:27.100
I hate this!

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:29.000
Dear, are you all right back there?

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:43.430
The rats are in the bag!

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:45.900
We'll get the ship moving and finish them with one blow!

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:47.930
Roger! The white one's impressive.

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:50.360
Yes, he lacks for nothing as an opponent!

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:53.160
They've pulled back, but...

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:56.130
That Motorad cruiser will definitely come!

00:14:57.030 --> 00:14:59.230
V2's Boots look fine.

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:02.160
Dad and the others are checking the engines right now.

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:03.960
I'll leave the engines to you!

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.560
Right, but what about reloading the weapons?

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:08.500
I'll have Tomáš and the others handle it!

00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:10.560
Mrs. Jellines, I'm sending it up now!

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:15.630
I hate this place! I can never live here on Earth!

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:19.060
If you're just going to whine about it, get off the ship!

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:22.330
That's not fair! Look at that awful sight outside...

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:24.500
Dying and rotting is part of life!

00:15:24.530 --> 00:15:25.900
Warren's right.

00:15:26.330 --> 00:15:27.460
Shahkti?

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:31.860
We may as well be like the whales or the seals.

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:34.430
It's true, as long as we bleed like this, right?

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:36.060
We die and then we rot.

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:37.400
You're bleeding!

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:39.700
Of course. I got hurt.

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:42.500
But, the bones on the shore are sickening!

00:15:42.530 --> 00:15:43.660
That's...

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:46.230
It's because the Earth's environment...

00:15:46.260 --> 00:15:48.800
...won't allow animals to die naturally anymore!

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:53.300
If they could live well, they'd die naturally and not have that happen!

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:55.560
Live well and then die naturally?

00:15:55.860 --> 00:15:57.000
I think so, too.

00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:59.800
But the Earth isn't like that now.

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:04.030
Aren't we fighting to make an environment where we can live well?

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:07.360
You mean, the reason we're fighting...

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:08.760
...is to live life well?

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:09.900
Sis...

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:11.760
It's hard, isn't it?

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:14.830
Yes. But even after seeing...

00:16:14.860 --> 00:16:18.260
...his own mother's body torn apart, Üso is still fighting.

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:19.730
Üso's mother?

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:23.560
Maybe living well means living as well as you can.

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:24.300
Maybe.

00:16:25.660 --> 00:16:29.000
If we just stand around shaking, we're going to rot here, Martina!

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:34.900
Do what you can while you're alive, then die well.

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:41.100
Bikers don't fly!

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:44.230
Hit the guerrilla ship and the white suit with the Twinrads!

00:16:44.260 --> 00:16:45.460
Enemy fighter, approaching!

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:46.600
Open fire!

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:52.300
Renda! Cicely! Swat that fly!

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:54.630
This ship is heading to the island!

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:59.460
Why won't they give up?! In that case...

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:03.060
I'll come in low!

00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:06.500
What?!

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:08.400
Die, white one!

00:17:10.930 --> 00:17:13.760
Tough defenses... It's headed for the White Ark?!

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:21.800
Odelo, Tomáš, head around to the left and right!

00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:28.700
We have a duty not to get in the others' way.

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:30.330
Right. Let's go.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:37.330
Don't die, guys.

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:38.960
Second attack, incoming!

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:41.760
No, you don't!

00:17:43.630 --> 00:17:44.900
C'mon!

00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:52.060
They're using the waterspouts as shields?

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:53.330
So can I!

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:58.060
Using the waterspouts, huh?

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:00.000
What?!

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:02.930
Die, white one!

00:18:06.360 --> 00:18:08.000
Scary mouth! Scary mouth!

00:18:08.030 --> 00:18:08.860
What?!

00:18:11.760 --> 00:18:12.730
Lieutenant Renda!

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:16.600
One more time!

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:17.530
Right!

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:19.500
What?!

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:23.330
Cicely!

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:31.730
They have reinforcements out here?!

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:37.860
Open fire! Reinforcements, incoming!

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:40.730
The Federation Forces are here in the North Sea, too?!

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:42.460
Or is it the League Militaire?

00:18:46.830 --> 00:18:49.400
The Londonderry unit has moved against them!

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:50.530
The Federation Forces?

00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:52.060
Üso!

00:18:55.300 --> 00:18:57.430
I need to use this boat as my legs!

00:18:57.460 --> 00:18:59.460
Roger! Just don't get thrown off!

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:00.160
Yes, sir!

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:03.260
And now he's using it like that?

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:13.360
Miss Marbet!

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:23.630
They got the main gun! Where's the other one?!

00:19:25.400 --> 00:19:27.130
Let's try a point blank attack!

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:30.860
What?!

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:32.660
Die, you white bastard!

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:44.860
If they can't use their guns...

00:19:45.230 --> 00:19:47.100
You'll pay for killing my friend!

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:51.460
Die!

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:52.930
Renda, we're submerging!

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:53.830
I can't!

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:56.500
With our main gun destroyed and Federation reinforcements here,

00:19:56.530 --> 00:19:58.160
we're at a disadvantage!

00:20:13.530 --> 00:20:14.960
The enemy's retreated.

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:17.900
Another push, and they might have finished us.

00:20:17.930 --> 00:20:19.960
Is that one of Londonderry's ships?

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:27.030
That boat came for us?

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:30.060
They said they belong to Captain Gomez's old unit.

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:34.330
Even out here, there are people who help the League Militaire.

00:20:35.700 --> 00:20:38.900
It took a lot of checking, but man...

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:42.360
We even have two boys piloting the Gun Blasters.

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:46.330
Understood. Next time, we'll help, even without Gomez asking us to.

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:47.560
Thank you, sir.

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:50.760
See you. We'll be on patrol around here.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:52.260
Thank you very much!

00:20:58.100 --> 00:21:00.760
I can't believe how warm this campfire feels.

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:05.530
Yeah, it's warm and makes me feel good inside.

00:21:08.860 --> 00:21:10.060
All done.

00:21:10.100 --> 00:21:11.430
It was delicious.

00:21:12.800 --> 00:21:13.930
Happy now?

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:16.200
You feel the same, Odelo.

00:21:16.230 --> 00:21:16.930
Huh?

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:17.960
What's up?

00:21:21.030 --> 00:21:22.300
What's up?

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:26.730
You two don't mind the smell now, do you?

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:28.230
Yeah, now that you mention it.

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:30.800
Maybe that wave washed the smell away.

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:32.200
No, it didn't.

00:21:32.360 --> 00:21:35.560
But now that you're used to Earth, Warren can marry-

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:38.800
WHOA! Whoa! Odelo, have some more coffee.

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:39.830
No, thanks.

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:41.230
What is it, Warren?

00:21:41.260 --> 00:21:42.830
Nothing! Nothing!

00:21:42.860 --> 00:21:45.930
I'm just really glad you're used to how Earth smells, now!

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:52.630
Even if death is something normal...

00:21:54.430 --> 00:21:59.360
This hatred I now have in my heart... This desire for revenge...

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:01.030
Can I ever forget it?

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:35.660
With Europe right in front of us, BESPA attacks again.

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:39.730
Taking responsibility for getting everyone caught in the battle,

00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:42.730
Odelo goes above and beyond to fight them.

00:23:42.830 --> 00:23:46.530
Üso uses the V2's shield at maximum power...

00:23:46.660 --> 00:23:49.000
...to drive the Motorad ship away.

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:53.100
Next time, on Mobile Suit Victory Gundam:

00:23:53.430 --> 00:23:56.630
Next Episode DYEING THE NORTH SEA IN FLAMES
"Dyeing the North Sea in Flames".

00:23:56.630 --> 00:23:58.100
Please watch it!

00:23:58.100 --> 00:23:59.360
Next Episode DYEING THE NORTH SEA IN FLAMES
